From 1c5a1fccdcc8a946a47b7239bb9fbdb06b576acb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c-drew <101952850+c-drew@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:13:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Shaders: per-block texture tiling for LoD terrain quads

LoD terrain draws one quad per 2^L-block voxel with the block's sprite spread across it and
stores the voxel size in blocks in glintUV.x (block faces never use glint; glint reads are
gated on USE_GLINT_BIT). Hit shaders repeat the sprite once per block and scale the ray-cone
derivatives to match, so far terrain has block-sized texels and leaf cut-outs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014aGN7pt3GAnXQRSSREgQzx
